oma seat, but not enough to move the forecast materially.", "watch": "Whether national Democratic outside spending materializes at scale and whether Bice's debate avoidance becomes a sustained story could narrow the margin.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent Stephanie Bice (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Stephanie Bice seeks a third term in a central Oklahoma district that leans about nine points Republican. She holds an overwhelming financial edge, with roughly $2 million on hand compared with about $17,000 for Democrat Jena Nelson, a former teacher who won her primary in June. An independent-sponsored poll from late September showed Bice ahead by five points, the only public survey of the race.\n\nMost expert raters place the seat at Solid or Safe Republican, though a few call it Likely Republican, and prediction markets give Nelson roughly a one-in-eight chance. National Democrats have added the district to their target list and signaled investment, and Bice has so far declined to debate. Those signs of Democratic interest keep the race from being rated Safe, but the district's lean and the money gap make Bice a clear favorite.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0558, "margin": -10.29}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0638, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.1454, "margin": -7.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0909, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.1152, "margin": -7.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0488, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.099, "margin": -8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.1151, "margin": -8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0881, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.0678, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.0911, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.0833, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.097, "margin": -8.8}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.0712, "margin": -9.0}]}